# Ratchet for scripts/check_tests_ssot.py's chunk-invariance rule.
#
# One serializable streaming object per line (its `<p>_set_state` prefix),
# each with a reason, whose output has no test that it does not depend on how
# the input was split into calls (native/tests/dp_chunk_inv.h).
#
# THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Give the object a test (a dozen lines against the
# harness) and delete its line. A new streaming object gets the test; it does
# not go on this list. An entry that has the test now, or is no longer a
# serializable streaming object, is a FAILURE (stale), and an entry ADDED
# since the merge base is a failure too.
#
# `dp_resamp` is tested, but its call-relative positions (eq_ctrl_pos in
# test_resamp_core.c) obey a different law -- chunking MOVES the number by
# exactly the input count -- and stay a bespoke test.
#
# Burn-down: doppler#1896.   Derived, not curated:
#   python scripts/check_tests_ssot.py   # names every uncovered object
